{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531315-philadelphia-by-night","id":1531315,"title":"Philadelphia by night","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-22T15:50:26-08:00","id":1531315,"title":"Philadelphia by night","content":"When contemplating the somewhat-predictable \u2018British Invasion\u2019 dynamic in DARK COLONY, it struck me that a power dynamic between local Elders and Fledgelings where the former were traditionally greeted with \u201cThe British are Coming!\u201d whenever the younger generation wanted to pick a fight with their sires would have been far more entertaining.<br /> <br /> It then occurred to me to wonder which other US city of consequence might cultivate a comparable tension between local Kindred: as you might imagine, Philadelphia PA (A city second only to Boston in terms of it\u2019s association with the American Revolution, with an even more<br /> pivotal role to the creation &amp; early years of the United States AND an embarrassing experience of British occupation during the Revolutionary War) immediately came to mind.<br /> <br /> One feels that the first capital of the United States (Where 13 Colonies first came together as one nation and where it\u2019s Constitution was written) would be exactly the sort of city in which Kindred who served during the Revolution and the War of Independence (who didn\u2019t especially want to become<br /> Prince of their own cities) might set up a sort of \u2018veteran\u2019s home\u2019 and cheer each other up whenever they felt out of step with Modern Nights.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m imagining this as a place where \u2018Brother Jonathan\u2019 of the 18th century sired \u2018Billy Yank\u2019 of the 19th, who embraced children of the American Century who now presumably in their turn set their sights on Millennials - and every single one of them presumably bickering with their forebears about what it means to be a Real American (Hence that nasty little joke about the local Elders having been mostly born as British subjects \u2026 or on another continent).<br /> <br /> <br /> It has also struck me that Philadelphia - with it\u2019s Greek name, inception as a colony built on religious toleration, pivotal role as the city where the United States came into existence as a nation built on Classical foundations and where members of the educated classes made Revolution positively RESPECTABLE (By comparison with the militias and angry mobs in Boston) - sounds like EXACTLY the sort of city where Critias, Brujah elder of note, would have asserted Praxis (Before wandering off to Chicago).<br /> <br /> <br /> With all that in mind, I\u2019ve been thinking a bit on what the City lf Brotherly Love might look like in the World of Darkness - I would therefore like to ask that any reader who has knowledge of Philadelphia being mentioned in any past sourcebook or novel share that knowledge, so that I can work out how to incorporate that information into my version of things.<br /> <br /> Thank You in advance for your consideration and please feel free to share your own thoughts on the Liberty Bell\u2019s old hangout, even if you don\u2019t come armed with canon!\ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T04:42:43-08:00","id":1531344,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a way to grab what was the original book's ultimate weakness and mold a strength out of it, i definitely approve.<br /> <br /> Reworking the factions in that book as &quot;trans-domain&quot; alliances and &quot;regional&quot; power blocs resulting of social experiments across geographical, generational and/or clan lines - not to mention immigrant x american-born x native, freedperson x slave, among other subdivisions, ever more muddy &amp; redefined with the decades and centuries - could mesh well with such a perspective, imho.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Roman_Pendragon\" target=\"_blank\">Pendragon</a> as a childe of Critias twisted/gone astray with the centuries instead of that &quot;rival methuselahs that build an alliance of their childer, for reasons&quot; could work much better from that angle too (no ideas about Biltmore or Warwick, unfortunately).<br /> <br /> Edit: re-reading <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/William_Biltmore\" target=\"_blank\">his</a> backstory, it crossed my mind that something in the vein of cursed bard/sorcerer and reminiscences/commentary of the moral panic &amp; mob rule of the Salem Witch Trials could perhaps work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-23-2024, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T05:54:17-08:00","id":1531347,"title":"","content":"Speaking of continuity nods, i remembered <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Elsa_Linden\" target=\"_blank\">one</a> elder in the book happens to be a childe of another of Chicago's primogen. While no other such clear interconnections, it might be fun to look into it.<br /> <br /> Correction - there are also Mark Decker (from Milwaukee by Night) being embraced in one of the battles of the American Revolution, plus Tyrus and Horace Turnbull (both from Chicago by Night) were natives of the 13 colonies era (though Tyrus already had 130 years of unlife by the time it started), in case you are interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-23-2024, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T06:13:00-08:00","id":1531350,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a>, thank you for your kind remarks and for your help: I\u2019m currently looking through the White Wolf wiki and the pages of past threads on this forum to see if I can find anything relevant to Philadelphia, to Pennsylvania and to the Revolutionary War era.<br /> <br /> I was actually lucky enough to find <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a>\u2019s thread on the Mid-Atlantic region, which suggested some interesting ideas (While also suggesting that there\u2019s more to find out, albeit in books I don\u2019t currently have access to: 2 steps forward, 1 step back, eh?).\ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> <br /> One interesting thing I\u2019ve just stumbled onto is that Critias of the Brujah is described as arriving in the New World \u201cshortly after the Revolutionary War\u201d which makes me stone-cold certain that he was in Philadelphia (Greek name, largest city in the US, major port, centrally-located, Benjamin Franklin\u2019s hometown, Capital of the American Revolution \u2026 oh yes, Critias would be drawn like a crow to a motorway) at the time various interested parties were hashing out the US Constitution (Though it\u2019s unlikely he was able to sit in on the debates and discussions in person).<br /> <br /> He might even have lingered after Philadelphia ceased to be the capital (National and State), though it\u2019s possible that the election of that famous gentleman-scholar and plantation owner Thomas Jefferson would have drawn him to D.C. (Jefferson\u2019s curious mix of slaveholder, scholar and democratic idealist would have tickled the old Sophist\u2019s presumably-Platonic notions of a philosopher king, if nothing else).<br /> <br /> I wonder if Philadelphia was Critias\u2019 home away from home (The place he stayed whenever he needed a break from his current residence) for most of his American sojourn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T04:32:21-07:00","id":1532430,"title":"","content":"Any update? As a nursing student, I know how hard it is to write nursing essays and to solve this problem, I use this <a href=\"https://ukwritings.com/nursing-essay-help\" target=\"_blank\">https://ukwritings.com/nursing-essay-help</a> website to stay calm during submission time. To use their service, you have to first go to their website, select your requirements, and then, once you have ordered the essay, you only have to wait calmly. I trust them for my work. Thank me later for this advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28268-sanfordhahn","user":"SanfordHahn","date":". 03-20-2024, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28268-sanfordhahn","name":"SanfordHahn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T09:51:01-07:00","id":1532439,"title":"","content":"I mean.....<a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/373618/Philadelphia-by-Night\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...lphia-by-Night</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T12:52:44-07:00","id":1532445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SanfordHahn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531315-philadelphia-by-night?p=1532430#post1532430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any update?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit that discovering there was a sourcebook called \u2018Philadelphia By Night\u2019 rather stole my thunder - not least because I only have access to a very limited number of sourcebooks.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T01:06:56-07:00","id":1532483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531315-philadelphia-by-night?p=1532445#post1532445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit that discovering there was a sourcebook called \u2018Philadelphia By Night\u2019 rather stole my thunder - not least because I only have access to a very limited number of sourcebooks.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's also Dark New England on STV ( which is amazing ) but that hasn't stopped the New England thread here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T06:31:10-07:00","id":1532494,"title":"","content":"Well yes, but that\u2019s because there\u2019s a lot more for me to work with in the New England thread without being obliged to buy one or more sourcebooks!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually, with hindsight, I should have posted my own vague notions in the Mid-Atlantic \u2018sister thread\u2019 to the above: I only realised that there was such a thing after creating this thread.<br /> <br /> Hindsight, as ever, is 20/10!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}